cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it using the metadata below, and carry its evidence-typing caveat into your work: most acceptance rates and all desk-rejection rates in this release are estimates, not publisher-stated values."
type: dataset
title: "Journal intelligence dataset: acceptance rates, review times and desk-rejection rates for 57 journals, with per-figure evidence typing"
abstract: "Acceptance rates, review timelines, desk-rejection rates and submission limits for 57 journals across 23 publishers and 17 fields. The distinguishing feature is that every volatile figure carries an evidence type (official, reported, estimated), so a reuser can tell measurement from inference. That typing is also the dataset's main finding: none of the 57 desk-rejection rates is officially published, only 4 of 57 acceptance rates are reported by any credible source, and only 1 review time is official. The data researchers are told to use when choosing a journal is largely not published by the journals. Four columns (difficulty score, difficulty band, primary fit signal, primary rejection reason) are Manusights editorial judgments derived from pre-submission review work rather than third-party data. The panel favours journals researchers most often ask about and is not a representative sample of the literature."
